this is interacting with nature on a  whole new level  these guys have hacked nature to create  a beautiful artistic collaboration  between humankind and insects so how did  these artists get thousands of fireflies  to dance to their human tune the duo set  up about 40 LEDs in the forest and  programmed them to go on and off at  regular intervals the fireflies  responded by flashing back fireflies are  actually not flies at all they're  different kinds of winged beetles and  different species flash for different  reasons to warn off predators or to  attract a mate some species don't flash  at all Robin and Andre have chosen to  use a species of fireflies called to  optics maliki which are among the 1% of  fireflies that synchronize their flashes  in large groups they flash naturally at  regular intervals but if they notice  another firefly nearby flashing they'll  interrupt their own pattern and start  over again every time it resets the  neural cycles of those two individual  fireflies will become more closely  matched within a few cycles the two  individuals will synchronize and begin  to flash at exactly the same time  eventually the whole tree begins  flashing in unison this process is  called entrainment robin and under a  have basically used the fact that the  fireflies can't tell the difference  between another firefly flashing and an  LED light flashing to basically hijack  the synchronization process in the video  these guys have used technology to  imitate nature but then nature turn  around and imitated that technology  right back  [Music]  you
 

